  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 305 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nPrecipitation chances will end in the east Monday evening as \nthe upper level disturbance tracks into the eastern Dakotas. \nAfter dry conditions for the next 18 to 24 hours, a second upper\nlevel trough, will cross the northern Rockies Tuesday, entering\nthe western Dakotas Tuesday evening. With westerly winds \nexpected across the western half of the forecast area Tuesday, \nmoisture will be limited with the main precipitation chances \nover eastern portions of the forecast area. Beyond Tuesday \nnight, dry conditions are expected through Friday. Late in the \nweek, the deterministic GFS and EC solns develop a closed low \nover the Pacific NW. As this feature tracks east, precipitation \nchances will increase next weekend. ATTM the best chances appear\nto be over the eastern half of Nebraska, however, given the \ntrack differences of the mid level low late next week into the \nweekend, forecast confidence in this becoming reality is low \nATTM.",
